===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=tree|:inh|enm:stok|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|stok}}, from {{inh|en|ang|stocc}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*stokk}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*stukkaz||tree-trunk}}.

Modern senses are mostly referring either to the trunk from which the tree grows (figuratively, its origin and/or support/foundation), or to a piece of wood, stick, or rod. The senses of "supply" and "raw material" arose from a probable conflation with {{m|en|steck||an item of goods, merchandise}} or the use of split [[tally stick|tally sticks]] consisting of foil or counterfoil and stock to capture paid taxes, debts or exchanges. {{doublet|en|chock}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~|s|stocken<l:obsolete>}}

# {{senseid|en|any stored stuff or supply}} A [[store]] or [[supply]].
#* {{RQ:Aston HJL|Preface|The Italian adage is particularly applicable to translators from the Japanese. Even when they have a competent knowledge of the language they cannot possibly reproduce all the metaphors, allusions, quotations, and illustrations which form the '''stock''' of the Japanese author, and which are in great part unintelligible without a profusion of explanatory notes intolerable to the reader.}}
## {{senseid|en|goods in inventory or inventory of goods, for sale}} {{lb|en|operations}} A [[store]] of [[good]]s ready for sale; [[inventory]].
##: {{hypo|en|{{w|new old stock}}|<|deadstock#Noun}}
##: {{ux|en|We have a '''stock''' of televisions on hand.}}
##: {{ux|en|I checked in the back of the stockroom and found some more '''stock'''.}}
## {{senseid|en|a supply of anything, stored until used}} A [[supply]] of anything, stored until used; especially, such a supply that is ready for use.
##: {{ux|en|Lay in a '''stock''' of wood for the winter season.}}
## {{senseid|en|rolling stock}} [[railroad|Railroad]] [[rolling stock]].
##: {{ux|en|The Grand Trunk Railway had just purchased a large order of '''stock''' from the American Car and Foundry Company.}}
## {{senseid|en|stack of undealt cards, in a card game}} {{lb|en|cards|in a [[card game]]}} A stack of undealt cards made available to the players.
## {{senseid|en|Q103459}} [[farm|Farm]] or [[ranch]] animals; [[livestock]].
##: {{ux|en|Good '''ranchers''' must continually keep watch over the health of their '''stock'''.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1881|author=William Rowntrie Robertson|title=Reports on the Agricultural Conditions, Capabilities, and Prospects Of The Neilgherry And Coimbatore Districts|page=33
|passage={{...}} the open land is generally covered by a grass which grows in tussacs, and produces tufts of hard, crisp, pointed blades. '''Stock''' will never willingly eat this grass; {{...}}}}
## {{senseid|en|population of wild fish or game}} The population of a given type of [[animal]] (especially fish) [[available]] to be [[captured]] from the wild for [[economic]] use.
##: {{ux|en|The '''stocks''' of this fishery are recovering from overfishing, but the gains can easily reverse if our husbandry efforts lapse.}}
# {{senseid|en|equity in a company; capital of a company}} {{lb|en|finance}} The [[capital]] raised by a company through the issue of [[share]]s; the total of shares held by an individual shareholder.
#: {{ux|en|His grandpa had bought some '''stock''' in General Electric in 1905, and he refused to sell it ever after.}}
## {{senseid|en|price or value of equity in a company}} The [[price]] or [[value]] of the stock of a company on the [[stock market]].
##: {{ux|en|When the bad news came out, the company's '''stock''' dropped precipitously.}}
## {{senseid|en|share}} {{lb|en|especially|US}} A [[share]] in a company.
## {{senseid|en|reputation}} {{lb|en|figurative}} The measure of how highly a person or institution is valued.
##: {{syn|en|reputation}}
##: {{ux|en|After that last screw-up of mine, my '''stock''' is pretty low around here.}}
##* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=Jonathan Martin; Maggie Haberman|title=Who Is King of Florida? Tensions Rise Between Trump and a Former Acolyte.|date=2022-01-17|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/01/16/us/trump-desantis.html|passage=With his '''stock''' rising fast in the party, the governor has conspicuously refrained from saying he would stand aside if Mr. Trump runs for the Republican nomination for president in 2024.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220118122902/https://www.nytimes.com/2022/01/16/us/trump-desantis.html|archivedate=18 January 2022}}
## {{senseid|en|any of various securities similar to a stock}} Any of several types of [[security]] that are similar to a stock, or marketed like one.
# {{senseid|en|raw material, such as feedstock}} The raw material from which things are made, such as [[feedstock]].
## {{senseid|en|broth as base for further food prep}} {{lb|en|cooking|uncountable|countable}} [[broth|Broth]] made from meat (originally bones) or vegetables, used as a basis for [[stew]] or [[soup]].
##: {{ux|en|They make beef '''stock''' from the butchery scraps that they otherwise might not have used.}}
## {{senseid|en|Q11472}} The type of paper used in printing.
##: {{ux|en|The books were printed on a heavier '''stock''' this year.}}
## {{senseid|en|film stock}} {{ellipsis of|en|film stock}}.
## {{senseid|en|plain soap before coloring and perfuming}} [[plain|Plain]] [[soap]] before it is coloured and perfumed.
# {{senseid|en|stock theater}} [[stock theater|Stock theater]], [[summer stock]] [[theater]].
# {{senseid|en|trunk and main limbs of a tree; base from which something ramifies}} The [[trunk]] and [[woody]] main [[stem]]s or [[limb#Noun|limb]]s of a tree; the base from which something grows or [[branch#Verb|branches]].
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Job|14|8|9|Though the roote thereof waxe old in the earth, and the '''stocke''' thereof die in the ground: Yet through the sent of water it will bud, and bring forth boughes like a plant.}}
## {{senseid|en|plant that receives scion, in grafting}} {{lb|en|horticulture}} The [[plant]] upon which the [[scion]] is [[graft#Verb|grafted]].
##: {{cot|en|scion#Noun}}
##* {{RQ:Bacon Sylva Sylvarum|passage=The [[cion]] [[overrule]]th the '''stock''' quite.}}
## {{senseid|en|lineage; family; ancestry}} {{lb|en|by extension}} [[lineage|Lineage]]; [[family]]; [[ancestry]].
##* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=i|page=18|passage=UUhat, ſhall I call thee brother? No, a foe,<br>Monſter of Nature, ſhame vnto thy '''ſtocke''',<br>That darſt preſume thy Soueraigne for to mocke.}}
##* {{RQ:Guardian|url=http://www.theguardian.com/film/2003/nov/14/television|author=Jacques Peretti|title=You are a bad man trying to do bad things to Vincent|date=2003-11-14|passage=His hatred is not based upon whom these people are (like many rightwing Republicans, Gallo comes from immigrant '''stock'''), but how easily these people have come by success in America.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261018072606/https://www.theguardian.com/film/2003/nov/14/television|archivedate=18 October 2026}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Lewis Richard Farnell|title=The Cults of the Greek States|page=108
|passage=We may also conclude that as it was the Ionic ''γένη'' of the Attic tetrapolis who in the main achieved the Ionization of Athens, so it was a branch of this same '''stock''' that settled at Delos {{...}}}}
### {{senseid|en|superfamily or macrofamily of languages}} {{lb|en|linguistics}} A larger grouping of language families: a [[superfamily]] or [[macrofamily]].
# {{senseid|en|plant of genus _Matthiola_}} Any of the several species of [[cruciferous]] [[flower]]s in the genus {{taxfmt|Matthiola|genus}}.
# {{senseid|en|handle or stem of tool or weapon}} A [[handle]] or [[stem]] to which the [[working]] [[part]] of an [[implement]] or [[weapon]] is [[attach]]ed.
## {{senseid|en|shoulder rest for firearm}} {{lb|en|firearm}} The part of a [[rifle]] or [[shotgun]] that rests against the shooter's [[shoulder]].
##* {{quote-book|en|author=Tom Turpin|title=Modern Custom Guns: Walnut, Steel, and Uncommon Artistry|edition=2nd|location=Iola, Wis.|publisher=Gun Digest Books|year=2013|page=47|isbn=978-1-4402-3646-4|text=The most underrated component in building a custom gun is the metalsmithing. '''Stock''' work immediately attracts attention. Fancy checkering patterns, meticulously executed, are sure to elicit ''oohs'' and ''ahhs''.}}
## {{senseid|en|handle of a whip, fishing rod, etc}} The handle of a [[whip]], [[fishing rod]], etc.
# {{senseid|en|a major part of a machine}} Part of a [[machine]] that supports items or holds them in place.
## {{senseid|en|headstock of a machine}} The [[headstock]] of a [[lathe]], [[drill]], etc.
## {{senseid|en|tailstock of a machine}} The [[tailstock]] of a [[lathe]].
# A [[bar]], [[stick]]{{,}} or [[rod]].
## A [[ski pole]].
## {{lb|en|nautical}} A [[bar]] going through an [[anchor]], perpendicular to the [[fluke]]s.
##* {{RQ:Conrad Mirror of the Sea|chapter=IV|passage=The honest, rough piece of iron, so simple in appearance, has more parts than the human body has limbs: the ring, the '''stock''', the crown, the flukes, the palms, the shank.  All this, according to the journalist, is “cast” when a ship arriving at an anchorage is brought up.}}
## {{lb|en|nautical}} The axle attached to the [[rudder]], which transfers the movement of the helm to the rudder.
## {{lb|en|geology}} A [[pipe]] (vertical cylinder of ore)
# A type of (now formal or official) [[neckwear]].
## A [[necktie]] or [[cravat]], particularly a wide necktie popular in the eighteenth century, often seen today as a part of formal wear for horse riding competitions.
##* {{RQ:Maugham Of Human Bondage|chapter=[[s:Of Human Bondage/Chapter CXVI|chapter 116]]|text=He wore a brown tweed suit and a white '''stock'''. His clothes hung loosely about him as though they had been made for a much larger man. He looked like a respectable farmer of the middle of the nineteenth century.}}
##* {{RQ:L. Durrell Livia|page=417|text=His grey waistcoat sported pearl buttons, and he wore a '''stock''' which set off to admiration a lean and aquiline face which was almost as grey as the rest of him.}}
## A piece of black cloth worn under a [[clerical collar]].
# A [[bed]] for [[infant]]s; a [[crib]], [[cot]], or [[cradle]]
# {{lb|en|folklore}} A piece of wood magically made to be just like a real baby and substituted for it by magical beings.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A cover for the legs; a [[stocking]].
# A block of wood; something fixed and solid; a pillar; a firm support; a post.
#* {{RQ:Milton Poems 1673|Massacre|58|passage=When all our Fathers worſhip't '''Stocks''' and Stones,}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1655|author=w:Thomas Fuller|title=The History of Waltham Abbey
|passage=Item, for a '''stock''' of brass for the holy water, seven shillings; which, by the canon, must be of marble or metal, and in no case of brick.}}
# {{senseid|en|dullard}} {{lb|en|by extension|obsolete}} A person who is as [[dull]] and [[lifeless]] as a stock or post; one who has little sense.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Taming of the Shrew|I|i|passage=Let's be no stoics, nor no '''stocks'''.}}
# {{lb|en|UK|historical}} The longest part of a split [[tally]] stick formerly struck in the [[exchequer]], which was delivered to the person who had lent the king money on account, as the evidence of indebtedness.
# {{lb|en|shipbuilding|in the plural}} The frame or timbers on which a ship rests during construction.
# {{lb|en|UK|in the plural}} Red and grey bricks, used for the exterior of walls and the front of buildings.
# {{lb|en|biology}} In [[tectology]], an aggregate or colony of [[individual]]s, such as trees, chains of [[salpa]]e, etc.
# The [[beater]] of a [[fulling mill]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1842|author=Jam Bischoff|title=A Comprehensive History of the Woollen and Worsted Manufactures|passage={{...}}a somewhat rude machine called the '''stocks''', and consisting of a pair of wooden mallets, worked alternately by a cog wheel.}}

